# Research — web-phase-grid-spans (In progress phase grid, spanning parent cards)

Evidence-only. No proposals. All line numbers are from the working tree at
`igor.cwer/wip/web-task-workspace` (HEAD `d98189e`), `go test ./internal/web/` green.

### Task Slice

- The In progress column's current lane geometry: view model (`PhaseLaneView`, `newPhaseLanes`), markup (`_board.html`), CSS (`assets/input.css`).
- Where a card's phase comes from (`task.BoardSnapshot.Phases` / `PhaseInfo`, records → file-name fallback) and what of it reaches the view.
- Nesting rules that decide which cards are roots and which are `CardView.Subtasks`, since a spanning card's range is defined over that group.
- The count invariants the column header and the lane headers carry today, and the tests that pin them.
- Narrow-column degradation (container query), the committed-CSS build step, and the test families that will break on any markup or class change.
- Not researched: service mutation paths, routes, workspace chain/tiler, Done statistics.

### Confirmed Facts

**Phase data (source)**

- `BoardSnapshot.Phases` holds a phase **only for in-progress tasks**, subtasks included; a missing entry is documented to read as `PhaseResearch` (`internal/task/view.go:33-37`), which holds because `Phase.Order()` maps anything unknown — the empty `Phase` included — to 0 (`internal/task/phase.go:87-89`).
- It is filled per task: if the `*.phase` records summarize to a current phase, that wins and `PhaseInfo[id]` is also set; otherwise the attached file names decide via `phaseFromFiles` (`internal/task/view.go:94-105`). Todo and done tasks are never read, so at most four small file reads per in-progress task per snapshot (`internal/task/view.go:38-40`, `:94`).
- The file-name fallback maps `task`→research, `research`→design, `design`→planning, `plan`/`implementation`→implementation, furthest wins, case-insensitive, one optional `.md` stripped, no marker at all = research (`internal/task/phase.go:96-116`).
- Workflow order and the four phases are `task.Phases()` (`internal/task/phase.go:23-30`); `Order()` is the index into it.

**View model (current)**

- `ColumnView.Lanes` is set for In progress only and is documented to *partition* `Cards` (`internal/web/view.go:52-54`, assignment `internal/web/view.go:403-412`).
- `PhaseLaneView` is `{Phase, Count, Cards}`; the comment states `Phase` names both the `lane-<phase>` class and the `data-phase` attribute, and `Count` counts in-progress tasks on its cards, nested subtasks included, so lane counts add up to the column's (`internal/web/view.go:135-144`).
- `newPhaseLanes` puts a card in **one** lane: `rank = max(own phase order, order of each nested in-progress subtask)`, i.e. the furthest phase of the group; a nested **todo** subtask neither ranks nor counts there because it has its own To do card (`internal/web/view.go:434-458`).
- `ColumnView.Count` is independent of the lanes: it counts every snapshot task with that status, subtasks included (`internal/web/view.go:392-400`).
- Nesting: a card nests in its parent when parent and child share a status; additionally a **todo** subtask of an in-progress parent nests *and* keeps its own To do card (`internal/web/view.go:366-385`). Nested cards are sorted and copied into `CardView.Subtasks` (`internal/web/view.go:385-388`), declared at `internal/web/view.go:186-189`.
- A `CardView` carries a single `Phase` string (plus `PhaseBy`/`PhaseAgo`/`PhaseOpen`), set **only** from `PhaseInfo`, i.e. only when the task has readable records — the file-name fallback never reaches the card (`internal/web/view.go:174-180`, `internal/web/view.go:603-614`). There is no field for a phase rank, a phase span, or a per-subtask lane anywhere in the view model (`internal/web/view.go:145-192`).
- Nested subtask `CardView`s are built by the same `newCardView`, so an in-progress nested subtask with records does carry `Phase` — the card template just never renders it for nested rows (`internal/web/view.go:359-362`, `internal/web/templates/_card.html:39-52`).
- Cards get `Href`/`HXGet` only in a detail view's subtask rows; board cards leave them empty and `_card.html` builds its own panel link (`internal/web/view.go:160-165`, `internal/web/templates/_card.html:2-7`).

**Markup (current)**

- The column body is the scroll container and carries `data-pane="column:<status>"`; `_board.html` branches `.Lanes` → `.Stats` → cards (`internal/web/templates/_board.html:23-50`).
- A lane is `<section class="lane lane-{{ .Phase }}" data-phase="{{ .Phase }}">` with a header (label + count chip) and, only when non-empty, a `flex flex-col gap-2` card stack — so an empty lane is a header-only stub (`internal/web/templates/_board.html:26-38`).
- The board grid is `md:grid-cols-3` with `xl:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,2fr)_minmax(0,1fr)]`, i.e. In progress is half the board from `xl` (`internal/web/templates/_board.html:13`).
- Nested subtask rows are a `border-l … pl-2` list inside the card, each row a link with a status dot, id, title, optional blocked chip and priority chip; no phase, no offset (`internal/web/templates/_card.html:37-54`).

**CSS (current)**

- `.lanes` is a vertical flex stack and an inline-size container; `--lane-min: 11rem`, `--lane-step: clamp(0px, (100% - var(--lane-min)) / 3, 20%)` (`internal/web/assets/input.css:69-74`).
- `.lane` offsets with `margin-left: calc(var(--lane,0) * var(--lane-step))` and narrows with `width: calc(100% - 3 * var(--lane-step))`; `--lane` is 0..3 from `.lane-research|design|planning|implementation` (`internal/web/assets/input.css:75-83`). It is `margin-left` on a flex column, not grid placement.
- `@container lanes (width < 14rem)` drops the indent and the width clamp entirely (`internal/web/assets/input.css:84-86`).
- The only `grid-column` in the project is the detail view's phase-run note (`internal/web/assets/input.css:90-92`); no `subgrid` anywhere (grep over `input.css` + `templates/`).
- Everything lives inside one `@layer components` block (`internal/web/assets/input.css:22`, closing `:266`).

**Build step**

- `scripts/build-css.sh` is a maintainer-only step (never `go build`/`go test`), pinned to Tailwind standalone v4.3.3, minified, writing the committed `internal/web/static/app.css` (`scripts/build-css.sh:1-19`, `:47`).
- Tailwind scans **only** `../templates` (`@import "tailwindcss" source(none)` + `@source "../templates"`, `internal/web/assets/input.css:13-15`), so a class assembled in Go would be dropped; the comment states this is why styles are named classes (`internal/web/assets/input.css:6-11`, repeated at `:196-198`).

