**Prior decisions recorded for the current lanes** (`tasks/in-progress-phase-columns/`)

- A **5-track grid where lane k spans tracks k+1…k+2** was considered and rejected then, for having no minimum width and no compressed mode — "it can only be literal or collapsed" (`tasks/in-progress-phase-columns/design:527`).
- A 2×2 / stacked sub-column layout was rejected by the user in favour of overlapping virtual lanes (`tasks/in-progress-phase-columns/design:523-524`).
- Value-named classes were chosen over an inline `style="--lane: N"` although html/template would allow the latter (`tasks/in-progress-phase-columns/design:288`).
- Empty lanes as header-only stubs was a deliberate decision with three stated reasons (`tasks/in-progress-phase-columns/design:232`).
- The `xl` 1:2:1 board grid exists to make the staircase legible; dropping it leaves 30–65 px steps (`tasks/in-progress-phase-columns/design:223`, `:251-256`).

